Q: NSNotificationCenter one post causes observers to be called twice A: <p>I came here for a similar bug in SwiftUI, hopes can help others,</p>
<p>I did register notification on init, hoping we wil add once:</p>
<blockquote>
<pre class="lang-none prettyprint-override"><code>
struct ContentView: View, DropDelegate {
    internal init()
        registerIconDragNotification()
    }



But when issued the notification, I was Called twice.

After some debug, I discovered the init is called TWICE, 
as (maybe ..) Swift re-created the Views BUT we have 
the OLD notification present.
(and I think old view was NOT released 
as kept alive (retained) by previous registration.

BAD Patch...


struct ContentView: View, DropDelegate {

    internal init() {
        if Self.alreadyRegisterd == false{
            registerIconDragNotification()
            Self.alreadyRegisterd = true
        }
    }


    // bad patch:
    private static var alreadyRegisterd = false

...

}
</code></pre>
</blockquote>
